## Run

```bash
make serve
curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/q/health/ready
```

`make serve` builds the application into `target/quarkus-app/` and runs it in the foreground until Ctrl+C. Settings come from the environment; see [docs/configuration.md](docs/configuration.md).

## API

<!-- stacks:fill The resources this service exposes, one line each, and who calls them. -->

[docs/http-api.md](docs/http-api.md) has the routes, the error envelope and the status table. The running service serves its OpenAPI document at `/q/openapi`.

## Development

Requires the JDK named in `.java-version` (on macOS, `brew install openjdk@<major>`; the Makefile finds it) and make. Maven comes from the committed wrapper, `./mvnw`.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make build` | The application in `target/quarkus-app/` |
| `make test` | Unit tests and `@QuarkusTest` HTTP tests |
| `make test-integration` | The packaged application as its own process, over real HTTP |
| `make fmt` | Format with Spotless |
| `make ci` | Everything CI runs |

See [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for how the code is laid out.

